Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||12-17-2001||03:40 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ontario.gif">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ontario2.gif">  <P>This is our 66 Corvair Corsa stuffed with a 215 Olds , punched to 263 Cu In. 320lbs complete , the motor runs backwards via a lunati cam.<P>Fun Fun Fun.<P>MintGreen , what was the starter relocation problem? I have a few 215's out in the garage as well. I think it would be great in the fiero. But after seeing what it takes to build one that makes a lot of HP , I know it's an expensive route.<P>Nice motors , spins to 7500rpm with little trouble.<P><BR>I believe I do have that article around here, do youhave a fax or mailing address? I don't want to sell it but Iwould be more than happy to send you a copy.<P>JM <BR>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, Big Bore TB, 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 12-17-2001).]||||reg||1
